# Assess product knowledge before a feature

Before proposing, designing, or implementing a feature, read `product-knowledge.md` and state the fit in the reply. Do this before writing code or a plan.

Name one primary use case:

- Admin onboarding: setup, configuration, integrations, permissions, rollout
- Trial conversion: reach value in the trial window and capture intent plus blockers
- End-user onboarding: role-based first workflow after an invite
- Technical product support: diagnose, guide the next step, escalate with context

Then say which outcome the feature serves: guided start, AI doing the repeatable work, a human kept for judgment or escalation, or trust. If none fit, say so and stop. Do not build a feature that sits outside those use cases.

```text
Use case: End-user onboarding
Fit: Helps the invited user complete the first workflow
Outcome: Guided start
```

```text
Use case: none
Fit: Adds a planner that chooses among imagined next clicks
Outcome: none — Kulu already knows the next step from the screen
```
